+# Final review, cluster 7 (model), epic hg-k4l
+
+Source: base 0dbe4772f4cd541e6b5ecaa1dd55b9a72f62c784, head efc21b65eb225578d3a623b29f23b3688849ea8b (both verified with `git rev-parse --verify <sha>^{commit}`). Caller checkout observed at HEAD efc21b65, working tree clean, before and during the review; nothing in the caller checkout was modified. Review source binding (`bind-review-source`) exited 0.
+
+Files: src/model/change.rs, effective.rs, graph.rs, manager.rs (new), mod.rs, seat.rs, teamspace.rs, tests.rs (slices 000042 to 000049). Read at head with `git show`. No tests were run; evidence for test results is the task reports in the digest (build requires the ht-build toolbox with a libz shim).
+
+## Spec conformance
+
+- §4.6 data model: `SeatRecord.manager`, `TeamspaceRecord.default_manager` and `GraphRecord.node_manager_seat` are `Option<SeatId>` with `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]`; no schema bump. `manager_fields_default_and_skip` and the round-trip tests prove absent-field parsing and omission on write (Global Constraints satisfied).
+- §4.6 precedence: `Pointers::effective_manager` implements live node manager -> None; explicit `manager`; teamspace `default_manager` when not the seat itself; else `live_node_manager()`. An explicit manager or default naming a seat absent from the tree is `Integrity` via `unresolved`; a missing or retired `node_manager_seat` is unassigned (None), not an error, as specified.
+- Retired transparency: `ancestors` walks through retired seats and `manager_chain` filters them out, so a stale pointer to a retired seat never yields integrity. `Pointers::load` uses `layout::all_seats`, which iterates both live and `archive/teamspaces` and both `seats` and `archive/seats`, so archived seats are "existing" and transparent rather than integrity. Verified in src/store/layout.rs at head.
+- Cycle detection: visited set in `ancestors`; error is `Integrity` with a reason naming the walk. `cycle_from` returns the loop slice (including a pre-existing loop downstream of a subject) for the would-create-cycle check.
+- `nearest_surviving_manager` (§4.11): first live ancestor not in the retiring set; with the node manager unretirable this terminates at the node manager when assigned.
+- §4.2 / B4: `referenced_seat_template` now raises `Integrity` (holder = member id, field `seat_template`) for missing, wrong-kind and team-structure templates, replacing the `Corrupt` arms. Plan-time callers (template create/copy dependencies) still surface `PlanError::Store` as `internal` through src/plan/commands.rs:39, so a user-supplied bad reference in a plan is not mislabelled as a committed-graph integrity failure; bootstrap tests 3642-3673 cover all three variants at the seat.resolve seam.
+- §4.7 registry: `RequestKind::ManagerEdit` and `NodeManagerSet` added.
+
+## Requirement baseline trace (cluster share)
+
+- B5 (optional manager pointer, reference to a seat): delivered here as the record fields and resolver; the CLI and plan producers (`manager set|clear`) are the plan/cli clusters' and the seam reviewer's to trace.
+- B8 (node manager has no parent): `effective_manager` returns None for the live node manager even when its record carries an explicit manager or its teamspace has a default (test `node_manager_has_no_manager`). The "cannot be retired" half lives in plan::managers::retire and observe; seam reviewer.
+- B9 (who/show display the chain): `manager_chain` supplies the data; rendering in threads/bootstrap/cli is the seam reviewer's.
+- B6 (reparent to retired seat's parent): `nearest_surviving_manager` supplies the target; the rewrite in `do_retire_seat` is the plan/observe clusters'.
+- B4: model-side mapping delivered as above.
+- Key abstraction "callers never read the pointer fields to decide who someone's manager is": a grep at head finds direct field reads only in plan::managers (record rewrites, which the spec assigns there) and first_seat's literal "node_manager_seat is unset" qualification test; none re-derive the precedence rule.
+
+## Findings
+
+- none
+
+## Concerns
+
+- src/model/manager.rs `ancestors`: the cycle error uses the walk's starting seat as `holder` and always `field = "manager"`, even when the loop is entered further up or closes through a teamspace default; the message's walk text is correct, so this only affects the structured holder/field.
+- src/model/manager.rs `nearest_surviving_manager`: computes the full ancestor list before searching, so an unresolvable pointer or cycle above the nearest live survivor turns a resolvable reparent target into an integrity error (observed cascades then fall back to the node manager instead of the true nearest survivor). Only reachable after out-of-band edits.
+- src/model/manager.rs `cycle_from`: `while let Ok(Some(n))` ends a walk silently on an integrity error (already recorded as a deferred minor for hg-k4l.4); safe only because ManagerEdit validates targets and other callers report missing pointers via `manager_chain`.
+- A seat whose `teamspace` id has no teamspace record is resolved as if the teamspace had no default (silently falls to the node manager) rather than as integrity; only reachable through out-of-band corruption since seats are enumerated from teamspace folders.
+
+## Verdict
+ready
+
+## Must fix before landing
+- none
