+## Untested scope
+- src/model/manager.rs: no unit test for `cycle_from` returning a loop that does not contain the subject (split_off at a non-zero index), nor for `effective_manager` on an unknown seat id (holder/field `seat`).
+- src/model/manager.rs: `PointerEdit::Live`, `DefaultManager` and `NodeManager` applications are exercised only through plan::managers::cycle_guard tests, not in the model unit tests.
+- src/model/manager.rs: `Pointers::load` is unit-tested only on an empty instance; loading real records with pointers (archived seats and archived teamspaces included) is covered only indirectly by plan and bootstrap tests.
+- src/model/manager.rs: no test for a retired seat used as a teamspace `default_manager` (transparency through the default edge) or for `nearest_surviving_manager` when every ancestor is retiring or none is assigned (returns None).
+
+## Deferred OK
+- Cycle integrity error reports the starting seat as holder and `manager` as field regardless of which edge closes the loop; message text is correct.
+- `nearest_surviving_manager` errors on corruption above the nearest live survivor instead of returning that survivor; out-of-band only, observed path falls back to the node manager.
+- Seat with a dangling teamspace id silently skips the default rather than raising integrity; out-of-band only.
